course: dictionary
lesson: 15738
title: Changing into something new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Transmute is a formal word. It means to change something completely into something different, in its form or in its nature. A tadpole does not just get bigger. It changes so much that it becomes a frog.
explain: Look for the clue words around it. «Over the summer, the tadpole slowly transmuted into a frog.» The word slowly tells you the change took time, and the word into tells you what the tadpole became. Transmute is often followed by into.
explain: Long ago, alchemists tried to transmute cheap metals, such as lead, into gold. Today, scientists use the word about real changes in matter. In a nuclear reaction, one element can be transmuted into another. Use the same check as always: swap in a simpler word like change, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Transmute means to change something completely into something different.
fact: The word is often used with into, as in «transmute into».
fact: «The alchemist hoped to transmute lead into gold.» Alchemists were early scientists who tried to do this.
fact: In modern science, transmutation means one chemical element changing into another.
fact: «Transmute» is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in books, history and science lessons.
exercise: «Over the summer, the tadpole slowly transmuted into a frog.» What did the tadpole do? | Swam faster than before | Sank to the bottom of the pond | Stayed exactly the same | *Changed completely into a different creature
exercise: «The alchemist hoped to transmute lead into gold.» What did the alchemist want to do? | Sell lead to a jeweller | *Change lead into gold | Melt lead and pour it into a bucket | Polish a lump of lead until it shone
exercise: Alchemists tried to ____ cheap metals into gold. Which word fits the gap? | Polish | Weigh | *Transmute | Measure
test: «Her sadness was transmuted into joy when her team won.» What does this sentence mean? | She was sad about the game | Her sadness got bigger | *Her sadness changed completely into joy | She forgot how to smile
test: In modern science, what can transmute one element into another? | Stirring a pot | Shaking a bottle of water | Melting ice | *A nuclear reaction
exam: Which phrase means the same as transmute? | *Change completely into something different | Hide away quietly | Count slowly to ten | Sleep soundly all night
